# Byte-reproducibility: the compilers under tools/ write LF, and
# src/core/provenance.test.ts byte-compares their output against the committed
# sidecars. A host with core.autocrlf=true (this one: system gitconfig) would
# otherwise check the multi-line JSON sidecars out with CRLF and break that
# compare on a fresh clone. Pin LF for every text file, independent of host config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Compiled outputs and compiler inputs: always text, always LF, never guessed.
*.json text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.tsx  text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalised.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.glb  binary
*.woff2 binary
